{"id":"155000003550","t":"Adding Unassigned Calendars to Groups","c":"48000449585","f":"155000000690","cn":"Calendars & Appointments","fn":"Calendar Groups (5)","m":"Wed, 14 May, 2025 at 10:18 AM","lm":"Wed, 14 May, 2025 at 10:18 AM","v":2,"w":67,"html":"\n            <p><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/yN1yhrhrmMA?&amp;wmode=opaque\" loading=\"lazy\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p><p>You can now assign Groups to the <strong>Unassigned Calendar</strong> type as well as other <strong>Round-robin</strong> Calendars</p><p>Go to <strong>Settings&gt; Calendars:</strong><br><strong><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/48275919878/original/gUC1FoTf1TkFGD4EjVwNtoSiNONwucJNGw.png?1673969124\" loading=\"lazy\"></strong></p><p>Click on the <strong>3 dots</strong> on the right side of the desired Calendar and then click on <strong>Move to Group</strong>:</p><p><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/48275920143/original/IaGc2orq1dFPZYTiaRHLr7vXXpmjMra8hA.png?1673969175\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>It would open a pop-up where you would be asked to select a group you want to assign to the calendar and then Click on <strong>Select</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/48275920666/original/1F0J1bCyUySo4ajbnqGnMjKzfasxNqZjOw.png?1673969263\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>\n            \n\n\n\n          "}